#### Validation Rule Definition

Validation rules are defined using JSON Schema or Avro schema specifications with custom validation attributes:

```json
{
  "type": "record",
  "name": "CustomerOrder",
  "namespace": "com.example.orders",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "orderId",
      "type": "string",
      "validation": {
        "required": true,
        "pattern": "^ORD-[0-9]{10}$",
        "errorMessage": "Order ID must match format ORD-XXXXXXXXXX"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "customerId",
      "type": "string",
      "validation": {
        "required": true,
        "pattern": "^CUST-[0-9]{8}$"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "orderDate",
      "type": "long",
      "logicalType": "timestamp-millis",
      "validation": {
        "required": true,
        "min": 1577836800000,
        "max": 4102444800000,
        "errorMessage": "Order date must be between 2020 and 2100"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "orderAmount",
      "type": "double",
      "validation": {
        "required": true,
        "min": 0.01,
        "max": 1000000.00,
        "errorMessage": "Order amount must be between $0.01 and $1M"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "orderStatus",
